{"id":"amminadab","name":"Amminadab","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:amminadab"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Amminadab","text":"Kindred of the prince. (1.) The father of Nahshon, who was chief of the tribe of Judah (Num. 1:7; 2:3; 7:12, 17; 10:14). His daughter Elisheba was married to Aaron (Ex. 6:23). (2.) A son of Kohath, the second son of Levi (1 Chr. 6:22), called also Izhar (2, 18). (3.) Chief of the 112 descendants of Uzziel the Levite (1 Chr. 15:10, 11)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H5992","lemma":"עַמִּינָדָב","xlit":"ʻAmmîynâdâb","gloss":"Amminadab, the name of four Israelites","kjv":"Amminadab","count":8,"share":0.67},{"strong":"H5177","lemma":"נַחְשׁוֹן","xlit":"Nachshôwn","gloss":"Nachshon, an Israelite","kjv":"Naashon, Nahshon","count":4,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H3205","lemma":"יָלַד","xlit":"yâlad","gloss":"to bear young","kjv":"bear, beget, birth, born","count":5,"share":0.42},{"strong":"G284","lemma":"Ἀμιναδάβ","xlit":"Aminadáb","gloss":"Aminadab, an Israelite","kjv":"Aminadab","count":2,"share":0.17},{"strong":"G689","lemma":"Ἀράμ","xlit":"Arám","gloss":"Aram , an Israelite","kjv":"Aram","count":2,"share":0.17},{"strong":"H7410","lemma":"רָם","xlit":"Râm","gloss":"Ram, the name of an Arabian and of an Israelite","kjv":"Ram. See also H1027","count":2,"share":0.17}],"verses":["Exod.6.23","Num.1.7","Ruth.4.19","Ruth.4.20","1Chr.2.10","1Chr.6.22","1Chr.15.10","1Chr.15.11","Num.2.9","Ruth.4.18","Matt.1.4","Luke.3.33"],"related":[{"id":"ram","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.19,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"nahshon","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.188,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"naashon","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.176,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"obed","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.13,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"genealogy","type":"cooccur","shared":6,"jaccard":0.031,"why":"6 verses are indexed under b